{
  "ref": "Job 22",
  "heRef": "איוב כ״ב",
  "isComplex": false,
  "text": [
    "Eliphaz the Temanite said in reply:",
    "<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">Can an individual be of use to God,</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">An intellect provide benefit?</span>",
    "<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">Does Shaddai gain if you are righteous,</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">Or profit if your conduct is blameless?</span>",
    "<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">Is it because of your piety that you are arraigned,</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">And entered into God’s judgment?</span>",
    "<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">You know that your wickedness is great,</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">And that your iniquities have no limit.</span>",
    "<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">You exact pledges from your fellows without reason,</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">And leave them naked, stripped of their clothes;</span>",
    "<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">You do not give the thirsty water to drink;</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">You deny bread to the hungry.</span>",
    "<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">The land belongs to the strong;</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">The privileged occupy it.</span>",
    "<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">You have sent away widows empty-handed;</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">The strength of the fatherless is broken.</span>",
    "<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">Therefore snares are all around you,</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">And sudden terrors frighten you,</span>",
    "<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">Or darkness, so you cannot see;</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">A flood of waters covers you.</span>",
    "<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">God is in the heavenly heights;</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">See the highest stars, how lofty!</span>",
    "<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">You say, “What can God know?</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">Is it possible to govern through the dense cloud?</span>",
    "<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">The clouds form an opaque screen</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">As [God] moves about the circuit of heaven.”</span>",
    "<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">Have you observed the immemorial path</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">That evildoers have trodden;</span>",
    "<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">How they were shriveled up before their time</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">And their foundation poured out like a river?</span>",
    "<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">They said to God, “Leave us alone;</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">What can Shaddai do about it?”</span>",
    "<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">But it was this One who filled their houses with good things.</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">(The thoughts of the wicked are beyond me!)</span>",
    "<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">The righteous, seeing the fate of the wicked,<sup class=\"footnote-marker\">a</sup><i class=\"footnote\"><b>the fate of the wicked </b>Heb. “it”; cf. v. <a class=\"refLink\" data-ref=\"Job 22:16\" href=\"Job.22.16\">16</a>.</i> rejoiced;</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">The innocent laughed with scorn.</span>",
    "<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">Surely their substance was destroyed,</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">And their remnant consumed by fire.</span>",
    "<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">Be close to [God] and wholehearted;</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">Good things will come to you thereby.</span>",
    "<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">Accept instruction from God’s mouth;</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">Lay up those words in your heart.</span>",
    "<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">If you return to Shaddai you will be restored,</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">If you banish iniquity from your tent;</span>",
    "<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">If you regard treasure as dirt,</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">Ophir-gold as stones of the wadi,</span>",
    "<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">And Shaddai be your treasure</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">And precious silver for you,</span>",
    "<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">When you seek the favor of Shaddai,</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">And lift up your face to God,</span>",
    "<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">You will offer prayer, and be heard,</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">And you will pay your vows.</span>",
    "<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">You will decree and it will be fulfilled,</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">And light will shine upon your affairs.</span>",
    "<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">When others sink low, you will say it is pride;</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">For [God] saves the humble.</span>",
    "<span class=\"poetry indentAll\">The guilty<sup class=\"footnote-marker\">b</sup><i class=\"footnote\"><b>The guilty </b>Or “The guiltless”; cf. Ibn Janah.</i> will be delivered—</span><br><span class=\"poetry indentAll\">Through the cleanness of your hands.</span>"
  ],
